# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows machines this repo is worked on, which
# would otherwise check these out with CRLF line endings. Shell scripts and git
# hooks with CRLF fail under Git Bash ("bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M", or every
# line erroring with "\r: command not found"), so the pin tooling would break
# on a fresh clone while looking perfectly fine in the diff. Force LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
